\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Constructed smooth forcing loops converging uniformly to zero whose nonlinear responses retain a finite drift, exposing missing iterated-integral data.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the full supplied definition, catalogue wording, source qualifications and listed references for 30005985. No fresh status or novelty search was performed. The argument below proves its auxiliary statements directly and does not import an unverified external theorem.

\paragraph{A vanishing-input instability test.} For integers \(n\geq1\), take smooth two-component inputs
\[
 x_n(t)=n^{-1/2}(\cos(nt)-1),\qquad y_n(t)=n^{-1/2}\sin(nt),\quad t\in[0,T].
\]
Both converge uniformly to zero. Drive the ordinary differential equations \(du_n=dx_n\), \(dv_n=u_n\,dy_n\), with zero initial data. Then \(u_n=x_n\) and direct integration yields
\[
 v_n(t)=\int_0^t(\cos^2(ns)-\cos(ns))ds
 =\frac t2+\frac{\sin(2nt)}{4n}-\frac{\sin(nt)}n.
\]
Thus \(v_n\to t/2\) uniformly, although the zero input produces \(v\equiv0\). Supremum control of the input alone cannot make this nonlinear solution map continuous.
\paragraph{Interpretation for unresolved scales.} The missing quantity is a signed iterated integral: the small loops retain finite area. This is an explicit reason an approximation of unresolved forcing may need more information than pointwise or uniform convergence. It does not imply that every climate closure requires rough paths; a linear additive equation would not have the same area sensitivity, and a spatially singular nonlinear PDE may require further renormalized products.
\paragraph{Source gap.} No specific geophysical equation, covariance or mesh perturbation law has been validated here. The first missing step is to determine which nonlinear products and iterated integrals survive the source coarse-graining and to prove stability in a topology controlling them. Suitable rough solution spaces, grid robustness and the choice among simple stochastic forcing and the advanced frameworks remain equation dependent, as stipulated in [S2].

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
